# wellfound-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore. Keep it there. A secret passed on a command line
# is readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history,
# which is why none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# So a `.env` never overrides something you typed, and an already-exported
# variable (a CI secret, direnv, your shell profile) is never clobbered by a
# file you forgot to delete.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below — smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions, because a documented-but-unread variable is worse than an
# undocumented one.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: on Wellfound there is exactly ONE thing you need, and it
# is the proxy below.
#
# Every route this scraper reads — /role/…, /jobs and /jobs/{id}-{slug} — is
# served normally to a residential exit and refused outright to a datacenter
# one. Measured 2026-09-17, three requests each: 200 from a 2captcha
# residential US exit, 403 from a Hetzner VPS on every route including
# robots.txt, to plain HTTP and to headless AND headful Chromium alike.
#
# So a proxy is not an optimisation here; it is the thing that makes the
# scraper work. Everything else below is optional.
#
# WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU BUY SOLVING FOR THIS SITE. Wellfound refuses in
# two skins and they are one decision by one vendor:
#
#   "Security Check | Wellfound"   the branded 403 a plain HTTP client gets
#   "Just a moment..."             Cloudflare's interstitial, for a browser
#
# Both are HTTP 403 and the first wears Wellfound's own name four times,
# which is why they are told apart structurally rather than by title.
#
# Cloudflare's challenge IS solvable — 2captcha builds it as
# `TurnstileTaskProxyless` — but it publishes no sitekey, because Cloudflare
# calls `turnstile.render()` once and keeps nothing. The engines hook that
# call before any page script runs; if no sitekey is captured they refuse to
# build a task rather than paying for one the API will reject. And from a
# residential exit there is usually no challenge to solve at all, which is
# the honest reason most runs never touch this key.
#
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API -------------------------------------------------
# A remote browser you do not run or patch, with a persistent profile and a
# chosen exit country. Used by --cdp-endpoint, and on this site it is what
# makes `--mode profile` work at all.
#
#   country-  picks the exit country. Use `country-us` (or `country-ca`):
#             Wellfound is a US site, and a datacenter address is
#             refused wherever it is. Measured: a `country-us` profile was
#             served normally where a German datacenter VPS got 403 on every
#             request, byte-identical over six polls.
#   pid-      is a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each,
#             capped per account — reuse pids rather than minting one per
#             run, and expect a 500 (`profile_locked`, exit 5) while another
#             run still holds this one. That is also why --concurrency is
#             refused with --cdp-endpoint: several workers would collide.
#
# Note that Selenium cannot use this: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress` takes
# a bare host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and pyppeteer
# authenticate on the WebSocket upgrade and work. selenium_scraper.py refuses
# a credentialed endpoint with exit 2 and says which engine to use instead —
# so a residential exit is what every mode here needs, not a specific
# engine.
#
# One more thing to expect: a credential here does not last. A Scraping
# Browser profile's login is good for about a day, which is why the canary
# workflow's gated job is dispatch-only rather than nightly, and why no
# working endpoint is ever pasted into this repo — only the SHAPE.
WELLFOUND_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-us-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy ----------------------------------------------------------------
# A residential exit. One URL here, or --proxy-file with one per line for a
# pool; a pool is what spreads a run's volume, and --concurrency without one
# just sends N times the traffic from a single address.
#
# This is the variable that decides whether this scraper works at all, and
# that is measured rather than assumed (2026-09-17):
#
#   from a datacenter address (Hetzner, Helsinki)   403 on EVERY route,
#                                                   robots.txt included, to
#                                                   plain HTTP and to
#                                                   headless AND headful
#                                                   Chromium alike
#   from a 2captcha residential US exit             200 on /, /jobs, every
#                                                   /role/… shape and
#                                                   /jobs/{id}-{slug},
#                                                   three times out of three
#
# Region: Wellfound is a US site, so `-region-us`. The country segment goes
# in the LOGIN and the gateway host is regional — `na.proxy` for the
# Americas, `eu.proxy` for Europe.
#
# The credentials here never reach the browser's command line — they go
# through the driver's own fields. Logs keep the host and port and mask the
# rest, because which exit a run used is the point of the log and is not the
# secret. Selenium's --proxy-server cannot authenticate at all, so that
# engine strips the credentials and warns rather than letting you believe a
# user:pass URL is doing something.
WELLFOUND_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@na.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- Default target -------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url. Wellfound serves ONE host in ONE language: there is
# no per-country TLD, no locale segment, and the exit country changes nothing
# about the markup — only whether you are served at all.
#
# The URL kinds, by mode:
#
#   /role/{role}                    --mode role. All listings for a role.
#   /role/r/{role}                  --mode role. The REMOTE listing, which is
#                                   a different listing and not a filter.
#   /role/l/{role}/{location}       --mode role. Role in one place.
#                                   All three take `?page=N`, and the page
#                                   they serve is twenty COMPANIES, not
#                                   twenty jobs.
#   /jobs                           --mode jobs. The discovery feed, served
#                                   at ONE address: `?page=2` returns the
#                                   identical rows.
#   /jobs/{id}-{slug}               --mode job. One job, from its
#                                   schema.org JobPosting.
#
# `/company/{slug}` is NOT here: it is Cloudflare-gated even from a
# residential exit, and this scraper has no mode for it.
#
# `--role` and `--location` build a landing URL for you, so this is optional.
WELLFOUND_URL=https://wellfound.com/role/r/software-engineer

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader — which only fills UNSET values — would
# never see it, and the variable would be silently inert: a setting that
# looks configurable and is not.
